  "notes": "Year = year of birth (children registered at birth in Italian municipal registers; ISTAT survey 'Iscritti in anagrafe per nascita'). Lists read from the data service behind ISTAT's own 'Conta nomi' calculator on the source page (years available 1999–2025). The calculator publishes rankings of at most the 50 most frequent names per sex (a request for more returns nothing), so each list has 50 names, not 100; order is by number of births as returned by ISTAT. ISTAT stores names in capitals WITHOUT accented letters and marks a final accent with an apostrophe: the boys' entry written here as \"Nicolo'\" is ISTAT's \"NICOLO'\" (i.e. Nicolò) and is kept as the source spells it. ISTAT counts each spelling/compound separately and states that the name data are for information only and are not corrected for spelling/transcription errors."
